  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: e9620f8c34305754d8cc9a7e49e852d9, type: 3}
  m_Name: Settings Hints_en-US
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Unity.Localization::UnityEngine.Localization.Tables.StringTable
  m_LocaleId:
    m_Code: en-US
  m_SharedData: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 2844a073f540ea44e87fd2f1554e23de, type: 2}
  m_Metadata:
    m_Items:
    - rid: 6739794259712409707
  m_TableData:
  - m_Id: 26665570304
    m_Localized: "- Each statue has red buttons on it, and they emit a Morse code
      sound signal that you can decipher from the book. They only activate when you
      solve the statue puzzle.\r\n\r\n- Correct sequence of symbols, starting from
      the left in the cryptex\r\n\r\n      <sprite name=\"Code Morse Correct symbols_7\"><sprite
      name=\"Code Morse Correct symbols_8\"><sprite name=\"Code Morse Correct symbols_9\"><sprite
      name=\"Code Morse Correct symbols_10\"><sprite name=\"Code Morse Correct symbols_3\"><sprite
      name=\"Code Morse Correct symbols_4\"><sprite name=\"Code Morse Correct symbols_5\">\n\n-
      You must confirm this sequence with the button on the counter located in front
      of the cryptex object."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items:
      - rid: 6739794259712409707
  - m_Id: 19533178097664
    m_Localized: 'A huge hall with many hidden puzzles. 20 of them, to be exact.



      If
      you climb the ladder and search the cabinets, you''ll find papyri, which are
      clues to the first puzzles you''ll be able to access.



      - Puzzle with
      12 rectangles

      Press the corresponding rectangles to open two gates.



      -
      Puzzle with swords

      You must place four swords in the appropriate slots
      next to the shields and other swords on the wall.



      Where there are
      many shelves with many items, you must find a papyrus that will allow you to
      solve the puzzle with the "up-down" buttons.



      - Puzzle with the "up-down"
      buttons

      The sequence of this puzzle is: down, up, down, up, down, down,
      up.



      PIPE PUZZLES



      - Skull and Bones

      You must move the
      bones and skull to the correct position, indicated by the same bone and skull
      symbol.



      - Sphere and Spinning Object Puzzle

      You must get the
      ball to the end of the maze.



      - 18-Gear Puzzle

      You must create
      a path from these gears and pipes from the upper arrows to the lower water
      canisters. You must create three separate closed circuits that lead to separate
      water canisters.



      - Clock Puzzle

      The currency symbols correspond
      to the Roman numerals on the clock. The same Roman numerals are on the pedestal
      below the clock. When you hold the appropriate symbol, you can examine it and
      see what symbol it represents. You must then match it to the corresponding
      pedestal, symbolized by the same Roman numeral as the currency symbol on the
      clock.



      - 4x9 Button Puzzle

      There are hidden symbols on the
      pipe and on the books, and their numbering must be reflected in this puzzle.

      The
      solution is TIHL.



      - Safe Puzzle

      A simple safe that works like
      a real safe. You turn the crank left or right.

      You must enter the appropriate
      code: right 13 left 35 right 72 left 5.



      - Hidden Button Puzzle

      In
      the bookcase, after you get rid of the books, hidden buttons and symbols next
      to them will appear, which are geometric shapes with the corresponding number
      of vertices. In the middle, you''ll find instructions on what to do: N-2, meaning
      you subtract 2 from the number of vertices on the symbol next to the button
      and click the button that many times. The order in which you click the buttons
      is also important, as indicated by arrows in the instructions. To see these
      symbols and buttons, you need to wear goggles.



      - Pickaxe Puzzle

      You
      must use the pickaxe on the wall to reach a hidden recess in the wall where
      the goggles are located. The wall you can destroy is located between the bookshelves
      and safe and the pipes in the corner of the room.



      - Goggles and Hidden
      Symbols Puzzle

      When you put on the goggles, you will begin to see symbols
      on the sliding tiles. There are four of these tiles, and each has an arrow
      pointing in a different direction to the wall with the symbols. But to solve
      the puzzle, you must select a symbol that is NOT on the wall and select it.



      -
      Skeleton and Knight Puzzle

      You must place the correct puzzle pieces
      in the correct spaces on the painting.

      The knight painting at the top
      must have a mace.

      The knight painting at the bottom must have a sword.

      The
      skeleton painting on the left must have an axe and a helmet. The skeleton image
      on the right must have a dagger and a Viking helmet with horns.



      -
      Gear Puzzle

      You must match the color of the door to the other color
      on another gear. If each color connects to a different color, the door will
      open.



      - Furniture Puzzle

      You move the furniture forward, backward,
      left, or right.

      You must lift the piece of furniture with the arrow
      to the spot where the arrow is on the ground.



      - Dark Puzzle

      You
      must discover the sequence shown by the two green flames in the distance. They
      represent four sequences of movement. And you must decipher it in the book.



      <sprite
      name="Morse Code Correct symbols_6"><sprite name="Morse Code Correct symbols_0"><sprite
      name="Morse Code Correct symbols_1"><sprite name="Morse Code Correct symbols_2">



      -
      Scale Puzzle

      You must balance the scale so that it shows the same weight
      on the left and right sides. There are 5 objects you can place on the scale,
      but you only need to place 3 of them, and the scale will show the same weight
      on the left and right sides.



      Weight, Cup, and Nail.



      - Diode
      Puzzle

      All diodes must be lit.



      - Two Brothers Puzzle

      The
      brothers lie or tell the truth, and the large statues of ABDI and ABDA have
      banners above them that describe something. You must look for these chests,
      bookshelves, prison cells, and hidden rooms. The solution is left, right, right,
      left, right.

      One chest is located right in front of the brothers'' statues.
      He says it''s true.

      The second chest is located right in front of the
      prison entrance. He says it''s a lie.

      There''s a chest in the prison
      that we don''t know what''s inside. We can''t see it, so it''s a lie.

      On
      the shelf are only books and a candlestick, so it''s true.

      And in the
      hidden room, there''s a chalice, so it''s true.

      Each hidden element
      has a symbol next to it, the same as the one on the banner.



      - Mirror
      Puzzle

      You must guide a beam of light to the appropriate crystal, located
      above the door.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items:
      - rid: 6739794259712409707
  - m_Id: 32678076502016
    m_Localized: "Another larger room with lots of puzzles. I counted exactly 16
      puzzles.\r\nExplore the entire room because there are many items you can pick
      up without solving any puzzles; you'll need them later. It's very important
      to focus on the card symbols: Heart, Diamond, Cross, and Spade.\r\n\r\n- Candlestick
      Puzzle\r\nThe first puzzle requires you to read the book and notice that there
      are larger letters in various places that tell you to pull the candlestick
      above the door.\r\n\r\n- Main Picture Puzzle\r\nYou must arrange the five symbols
      on the painting, which you will read about in the papyri and books while solving
      the other puzzles in this room.\r\nThe solution is: Mole, smiling face, club,
      yellow tulip, black medallion.\r\n\r\n- Connecting 12 Dots Puzzle\r\nYou must
      connect all the dots to create a closed circuit. There are many possible solutions
      to this puzzle. At least 4 different combination sequences, but there may be
      more. xD\r\n\r\n- Block Puzzle\r\nYou must press all the square buttons so
      that each button is pressed. The red squares are excluded from the puzzle and
      block your movement.\r\n\r\n- Crowbar Puzzle\r\nYou must take the crowbar and
      use it to open a broken cabinet containing an item needed to solve another
      puzzle.\r\n\r\n- Dice Puzzle\r\nYou must move two dice to their corresponding
      positions. They are color-coded. The bottom dice must be at the top of the
      board, and the top dice must be at the bottom.\r\n\r\n- Six-Wheel Puzzle\r\nYou
      must match the order of the symbols as shown on the banners. The color-coded
      banners indicate which circle has which symbol. They are arranged from left
      to right on the wall and in the puzzle.\r\n\r\n- Card Symbol Puzzle\r\nYou
      must reproduce the same pattern of symbols, but note that the pattern is wobbly
      because it broke from the chain, and you must arrange it correctly, taking
      into account the rotation of the hanging panel.\r\n\r\n- Pressure Plate Puzzle\r\nYou
      are given two different torn pages that provide the sequence in which you must
      press the pressure plates.\r\nThe solution is that the first pressure plate
      is located near the bells, the next pressure plate is immediately next to the
      entrance door to this room, and the last is located at the exit gate from this
      room.\r\n\r\n- Arrow Puzzle\r\nYou must reproduce the correct sequence of arrow
      movements from the first arrow to the last row.\r\n\r\n- Bell Puzzle\r\nEach
      bell has a model of the symbol from the card, and the symbols of these cards
      are revealed on the walls in the order given in the papyrus you previously
      unlocked.\nThe order of the symbols on the bells you must ring:\r\n     <sprite
      name=\"More Symbols For Text_5\"><sprite name=\"More Symbols For Text_3\"><sprite
      name=\"More Symbols For Text_2\"><sprite name=\"More Symbols For Text_4\">\r\n\r\n-
      Terrain Puzzle\r\nYou must pay attention to the clues written on the walls.
      They will guide you as to which symbol must be in which position in the terrain.
      These symbols are also compared in the order printed on the wall when the gates
      open.\r\n\r\n- 6 Rectangle Puzzle\r\nYou must slide each rectangle out of the
      puzzle, but be careful because they interlock, and you must pull them out one
      by one, clearing the way for another rectangle.\r\n\r\n- 3 Symbol Puzzle\r\nYou
      must find 3 symbols in this room, insert them into the puzzle, and arrange
      the symbol sequences. \nThe solution is:\r\n     <sprite name=\"More Symbols
      For Text_0\"><sprite name=\"More Symbols For Text_1\"><sprite name=\"More Symbols
      For Text_0\">\r\n\r\n- Maze Puzzle\r\nYou must guide the object through the
      maze to the location shown on the ceiling.\r\n\r\n- 16 Dot Puzzle\r\nYou must
      make all the dots turn on."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 45619555356672
    m_Localized: "- Search the bookshelf there\u2019s a key there that opens the
      door to the next room. In that room, there\u2019s also a book that unlocks
      the next room, but to get the book that\u2019s above you, you\u2019ll need
      to brew a flying potion."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 45970979311616
    m_Localized: '- There are hidden buttons on the wall in this room; you need to
      click them, and then a hidden compartment will open, revealing a lever that
      unlocks the door.



      - There is also a bag here that you need to cut
      open to get the key to the next room.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 46168715579392
    m_Localized: '- The room generally contains only a potion recipe and a bookshelf
      that unlocks access to the next room; there are branches leading to three other
      rooms.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 46400069193728
    m_Localized: "- You need to find a shovel and dig up the hammer, which you can
      use to smash the upside-down pot in the corner of the room. Then you\u2019ll
      get a key that opens the chests containing the knife you need to cut open the
      sack.\n\n- The spot to dig is on the right, halfway from the entrance; there\u2019s
      also a hint on the wall showing where to look for the spot to dig."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 46604335992832
    m_Localized: '- Immediately upon entering the room, there is a lockpick on the
      right that opens the door. In the center of the cell, you''ll find levers and
      a book listing the sequence for the three levers.


      - The next lever
      is behind the chair, and the fork on the table corresponds to the third and
      final lever.


      - Move the first and second levers down, and the last
      one up.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 46877116747776
    m_Localized: "- The main feature is a cauldron where you brew potions that grant
      you various effects.\n\n- Various ingredients are scattered around the room:
      meat, twigs, leaves, wine, blood, acid, and water.\n\n- There is also a desk
      that stores all your collected recipes and shows their contents and how to
      make a given potion.\n\n- Right now, you\u2019re interested in the flying potion\n-
      twigs, leaves, meat, wine, and water"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 47317971652608
    m_Localized: "- Take the lanterns, go through the maze, and look for the 5 items
      needed to build the numeric keypad that opens the door to the next room.\n-
      The first item is right at the start, in a chest as soon as you enter the maze.\n-
      Pass one intersection by continuing straight ahead, pass three chairs and an
      open barrel, then turn right; there you\u2019ll find a key on a chair and the
      second item on a bookshelf.\n- Keep going straight without turning anywhere;
      you\u2019ll find a bookshelf with four books, and there you\u2019ll find the
      third item.\n- Keep going straight again, and there you must use the key on
      the chest, which contains another item.\n- Now you have to go a very long way,
      but if you keep staying close to the left wall, you\u2019ll eventually reach
      the last item, which is in a chest.\n- Then, keep staying close to the left
      wall, and you\u2019ll reach the exit of the maze; the light will turn off automatically
      when you get there."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 47784936099840
    m_Localized: '- In the middle of the room is a workbench; there, you must build
      a numeric keypad to mount on the wall.


      - On the wall are symbols seen
      in the maze; calculate their vertices and enter them one by one into the numeric
      keypad.

      -3407'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 48091367755776
    m_Localized: '- The book with the Morse code is in the bottom drawer right after
      you go up the stairs.



      - The statues have books that describe their
      positions. You MUST start by reading the book next to the seated man statue
      because it explains what the horse statue should do, and once you position
      the horse statue correctly, the book next to the horse will show you the next
      statue and its position, and so on.



      - Once you solve the puzzle with
      the statues, they will show you the location of a hidden button in the wall.
      When you click it, the wall will slide open to reveal the Kryptex.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 48312529211392
    m_Localized: 'Correct positions of the statues

      - Seated male statue -
      N

      - Horse statue - E

      - Female statue with arms outstretched -
      N

      - Statue of a man praying - W

      - Statue of a man with a crown
      - S

      - Female statue with arms at her sides - E

      - Statue of a
      woman with her arm bent at the elbow - S'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 48793477468160
    m_Localized: "- Each statue has red buttons on it, and these emit a Morse code
      signal that you can decipher using the book. They are activated only after
      you solve the statue puzzle.\r\n\r\n- The correct sequence of symbols, starting
      from the left in the kryptex\n\n      <sprite name=\"Code Morse Correct symbols_3\"><sprite
      name=\"Code Morse Correct symbols_4\"><sprite name=\"Code Morse Correct symbols_5\"><sprite
      name=\"Code Morse Correct symbols_6\"><sprite name=\"Code Morse Correct symbols_0\"><sprite
      name=\"Code Morse Correct symbols_1\"><sprite name=\"Code Morse Correct symbols_2\">\n\n-
      You must confirm this sequence using the button on the counter located in front
      of the Kryptex"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 49235393531904
    m_Localized: "- Mirrors that reflect a beam of light.\r\n- You need to direct
      that beam toward the crystal located just above the door\u2014the large blue
      crystal."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 49836672176128
